  "about": "How a project's database is named and reached, shared by aisc_identity.projectdb and its JavaScript twin shared/access-ts/projectDb.mjs, so the copies in each service cannot drift. A pid names a database only in its canonical form (any case); a template is a URL with {database} as its path, its credentials percent-encoded; dsn() drops only Prisma's own options (schema, connection_limit, pool_timeout) and keeps every libpq option.",
